The CV content in data/cv.yaml and the personal image in
assets/images/avatar.png are not covered by this software license.

The PDF layout uses the MIT-licensed Alta CV Typst package:
https://github.com/smur89/alta-typst

Alta CV and its dependencies are vendored under vendor/typst/ so the PDF
build needs no network access. Each package keeps its own upstream
LICENSE file alongside its sources:

  vendor/typst/preview/altacv        MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 George Honeywood
  vendor/typst/preview/fontawesome   MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 duskmoon314 (Campbell He)
  vendor/typst/preview/gairm-import  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Shane Murphy
  vendor/typst/preview/zebra         MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Julian

Local modifications to the vendored sources are marked with a
"LOCAL PATCH (Bluesboy/cv)" comment at each change.

The web layout is adapted from the MIT-licensed Almeida CV Hugo theme:
Copyright (c) 2020 Inês Almeida
https://github.com/ineesalmeida/almeida-cv

The bundled Font Awesome fonts remain under their upstream license in
assets/fonts/LICENSE.txt. They are subset to the icons the vendored CV
theme can request; scripts/build_fonts.py reproduces them from the
upstream desktop package. The inline SVG glyph outlines in
layouts/partials/icon.html are extracted from those same font files and
remain covered by that license.

IBM Plex Sans is bundled in assets/fonts under the SIL Open Font License
1.1, Copyright (c) 2017 IBM Corp. The full license text ships alongside
it in assets/fonts/OFL-IBMPlexSans.txt. The bundled faces are static
instances cut from the upstream variable font and subset to Latin and
Cyrillic; scripts/build_fonts.py reproduces them from the pinned source. The inline SVG glyph outlines in
layouts/partials/icon.html are extracted from those same font files and
remain covered by that license.
